    {
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "**Where the numbers come from.** The workload panels (services, database, sweep, replicas, restarts) read kube-state-metrics. The model-call panels read the Model Gateway's call counter.\n\n**Nothing is notified.** Prometheus evaluates the alert rules in `infra/kind/alerts/meridian.yaml` and notifies nobody, because kind has no Alertmanager: the table below is where a firing alert shows. Every objective the rules defend is a proposal nobody measured, in `docs/operations/slo.md`.\n\n**How the share of answered calls is computed.** A gateway process exports its counters once a minute, and its first export already carries what it counted, so `increase()` and `rate()` would miss it. The panel subtracts each series' value at the start of the time range (zero for a process that started inside the range) from its last value. Choose a range of at least two minutes. The per-5-minute charts use the same subtraction over five minutes. A gap in the data (a laptop that slept) is bridged by taking each series' last value before the range. Prometheus keeps 24 hours on kind, so a longer range shows what it still holds.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "What this shows",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "The six services (claims-api, agent-runtime, model-gateway, policy-mcp, claims-mcp, knowledge-mcp) with at least one available replica. Six when every one of the six is up; the rate store has a figure of its own.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 6
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(kube_deployment_status_replicas_available{namespace=\"meridian\", deployment=~\"claims-api|agent-runtime|model-gateway|policy-mcp|claims-mcp|knowledge-mcp\"} > bool 0)",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "__auto",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Services available",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "1 when the rate store is up; the gateway refuses every model call without it",
